# DESK31 item 1 -- `d_dofileren` asks before it overwrites, run B: the same
# gesture as d31c, but the name conflict is answered with OK instead of Stop.
#
# `d_dofileren` is the same-drive MOVE (`Frename`).  Until DESK31 it was a bare
# `dos_rename`, so moving a file over one of the same name simply failed and
# the user was told nothing.  EmuTOS loops (deskdir.c:785-825): `item_exists`
# -> `get_new_name` (the ADCPALER name-conflict dialog) -> and, when the user
# confirms the name unchanged, `dos_delete(newname)` so the rename can succeed.
#
# The gesture:
#   1. open the C:\ window
#   2. drag the SUB folder onto the desktop -> a folder shortcut for C:\SUB
#   3. CTRL-drag C:\PROOF.TXT onto that shortcut.  Ctrl makes it a MOVE
#      (`drag_op`), the drive is the same, so `dir_op` turns OP_MOVE into
#      OP_RENAME -- and C:\SUB\PROOF.TXT already exists (both files are on the
#      standard card image, the DESK18 working-directory fixture).
#
#   B_WIN1       the C:\ window open
#   C_SHORTCUT   the SUB folder shortcut on the desktop
#   D_MOVEBOX    the ADCPYDEL box, now headed MOVE FILE(S)
#   E_NAMECON    the ADCPALER name-conflict dialog `get_new_name` puts up
#   F_REPLACED   its *OK* taken with the name unchanged -- the destination is
#                deleted and the rename succeeds
#
# Coordinates from the probe run: C: (38,35); 'SUB' (515,103) and 'PROOF.TXT'
# (95,271) in window 1; the free desktop cell (220,449).  Ctrl is IKBD
# scancode 0x1D (make) / 0x9D (break) and must still be down at the release,
# because the drop-time keystate is what `act_bdown` reads (deskact.c:681).
100 parkbr
300 move 600 240
1000 arm
1200 mark A_IDLE
1600 move 38 35
1800 down
1803 up
1810 down
1813 up
2400 move 600 240
3200 mark B_WIN1
3600 move 515 103
4000 down
4100 drag 250 458
4700 up
5000 move 600 300
5800 mark C_SHORTCUT
6200 move 95 271
6600 down
6603 up
7000 key 1d
7200 move 95 271
7600 down
7700 drag 200 350
8000 drag 220 449
8500 up
8700 key 9d
8900 move 600 300
10000 mark D_MOVEBOX
# -- OK the move box (229,301 from this run's [dlg] dump); the name conflict
#    follows.
10400 move 229 301
10800 down
11000 up
11600 parkbr
13000 mark E_NAMECON
# -- *OK* (223,301) with the name UNCHANGED.  That is `get_new_name`'s answer
#    `1`, and `d_dofileren`'s one real decision: `oldname != newname`, so
#    `dos_delete(newname)` clears the way and the `Frename` on the next turn of
#    the loop succeeds (deskdir.c:815-819).  Read back from the image:
#    C:\SUB\PROOF.TXT must now be the 19-byte root file and C:\PROOF.TXT gone.
13400 move 223 301
13800 down
14000 up
14600 parkbr
16400 mark F_REPLACED
